# Stress-testing a discontinuity
subtitle: "How to test a regression discontinuity: bandwidth sensitivity, density and sorting checks, and what a fuzzy jump ratio really estimates, on Medicare at 65."
tags: ["regression discontinuity","bandwidth","manipulation","fuzzy rd","medicare","causal inference"]
teaches: ["methods/regression-discontinuity","methods/bandwidth-sensitivity","methods/density-test","concepts/exclusion-restriction"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed","b":"gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow"}
next: {"title":"Building a counterfactual state: synthetic control and Proposition 99","href":"https://drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/dcast/causal-inference-in-economics-evidence-from-health-and-health-care/building-a-counterfactual-state-synthetic-control-and-proposition-99.cast"}

