  lines:
    male|a||Patients rushed into hospital just after their sixty-fifth birthday are less likely to die that week than patients rushed in just before. Is that Medicare, and how hard would we have to push before the claim falls over?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14560
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||The claim rests on one line: at sixty-five almost every American becomes eligible for Medicare, the public insurance for older people.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:5oi7zw'
    'male|a||These dots are made up, but close in size to the real study: each is the share of emergency patients of one age who died within a week.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1fyfpvh'
    male|a||The risk of death climbs with age, so the dots rise, but right at sixty-five they step down.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:hiw23u'
    male|a||Nothing else about a person's health should jump on that birthday. So a step exactly at the line is credited to the thing that switched there, and that is the whole logic of regression discontinuity.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:nh8vzg'
    'male|a||The quick way to measure the step: fit a straight line on each side, five years out, and read the gap where they reach the birthday.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:28mcxa'
    male|a||That gap is minus one and a half percentage points, with a 95 percent margin of four tenths.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1r13o8y'
    male|a||Before we change anything, a guess. Fit the same lines over just two years either side instead of five. What happens to the gap?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19ccm72'
    male|a||It shrinks, to about one point, because the far-away dots were tilting the lines.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Here are the two-year lines.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1720
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||The gap is now one point. Same dots, a different answer.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:r4dljy'
    male|a||Which one should we believe?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:brtepr'
    'male|a||The answer lies in the curve the dots follow: far from sixty-five it bends, and a straight line stretched over a bend tilts to chase it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tndtsr'
    male|a||Stretch the lines back out to five years, and watch each one swing away from the curve right where it meets the birthday.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:14pyzw7'
    male|a||So why not always look through a narrow window?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1guzbj8'
    male|a||At one year the gap is still about one point, but it rests on just two dots a side, and its 95 percent margin swells to almost nine tenths.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:x8hok9'
    'male|a||That is the trade every discontinuity makes: a wide window buys precision and risks bias, a narrow one cuts the bias and pays in noise.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:yyhdyp'
    male|a||And the window is only the first test. A discontinuity also breaks if people could choose their side of the line, or if crossing it changed the treatment for some people and not others.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1l7ink7'
    male|a||We push on each in turn, and see whether this drop at sixty-five survives.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17j7mkv'
    male|a||How wide a window should a discontinuity look through, when every width gives a different answer?:
      mp3: 
