    male|a||Real researchers cannot see a truth line, so they choose the width by rule. The rule Imbens and Kalyanaraman proposed in 2012 balances bias against noise, and in our made-up data it lands near three years.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 16120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:154fm3n'
    male|a||At that width the bias, about a tenth of a point, is not small next to a standard error of about a quarter, so the usual margin comes out too narrow.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kgqlzt'
    male|a||Calonico, Cattaneo and Titiunik showed in 2014 how to correct for that bias and widen the margin to match, like these darker lines, and that is now the standard report.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:6fsod'
    'male|a||The real study behind our made-up dots is Card, Dobkin and Maestas, 2009: about four hundred thousand emergency patients aged sixty to seventy, admitted to California hospitals between 1992 and 2002.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1dh800q'
    male|a||With a smooth curve on each side across the whole decade, and with controls for the patients, deaths within a week fell by one point at sixty-five, with a standard error of two tenths, from a base of about five percent.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11j4x6h'
    male|a||A straight line fitted close to the birthday, with a rule-of-thumb window, gave minus point eight, also with a standard error of two tenths.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xlv99h'
    'male|a||And a more flexible curve, a cubic, gave minus point seven, with a standard error of three tenths: the drop shrinks a little, but it never disappears.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ucxjx8'
    male|a||A new case. A scholarship goes to pupils above a test-score cutoff. Within 5 marks of it the gain in later grades is 4 points, within 10 marks also 4, and within 30 marks it is 9. Which belongs in the headline?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 15680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:243xr6'
    male|a||The 4, because it holds steady as the window changes; the jump to 9 at wide windows is the bend, shown beside it rather than hidden.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10920
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||So a discontinuity estimate is not one number but a curve, and the credible report shows that curve, not its most flattering point.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9560
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||A window can be chosen with care and a discontinuity can still fail, if people could decide which side of the line they landed on.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7720
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Nobody chooses a birthday, so age looks safe. But a hospital study counts patients, not birthdays, and a patient can sometimes choose when to come in.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:chlc5d'
    male|a||Take planned stays, a new hip or a gall bladder operation. Here is the number of patients at each age, set to one hundred just before sixty-five.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cc3dtj'
    'male|a||Just after the birthday the count jumps by about twelve percent, with a standard error of half a point: the shape here is drawn by hand, but that jump is the real study''s, from the same California hospital records.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2vk3py'
    male|a||Why would twelve percent more people need a new hip the month after turning sixty-five?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:o2s477'
    male|a||They don't. People with thin coverage put the operation off, and book it once Medicare pays.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1eq1cck'
    'male|a||So the patients just over sixty-five are no longer like those just under: the over side has gained people who would not have been in hospital a month earlier.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1d2lshr'
    male|a||Compare death rates across that line, and the effect of Medicare is mixed up with a change in who is being counted.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tiq0pc'
    'male|a||That is why the first test of a discontinuity ignores the outcome and simply counts: does the number of people jump at the line? Justin McCrary turned that count into a formal test in 2008.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:itodu1'
    male|a||Card, Dobkin and Maestas met the problem head on. They kept only emergencies that cannot wait, like heart attacks and strokes, the kind that arrive as often on a Sunday as on a Tuesday.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:l1h9zq'
    'male|a||For those, the count runs straight through sixty-five: a rise of six tenths of a percent, with a standard error of nine tenths.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1o65i1v'
    male|a||A smooth count is needed, but it is not enough, so they also checked who the patients were.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cgmnx6'
    male|a||Their other illnesses, and their risk of death predicted from age, sex, race and diagnosis, showed no jump at the line either.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1cegqlc'
    'male|a||So age passes, but only in the right sample. A reported income is like a booked operation: the person who gains from the line also controls the number.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lecz4r'
    male|a||A new case. Babies born under 1,500 grams get extra care. A count of births shows a spike at exactly 1,500. What is the likeliest reason?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:x1zdpz'
    male|a||Weights recorded as round numbers pile up at 1,500, so the babies in that spike may not be like the babies around them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||This is a live case. Almond, Doyle, Kowalski and Williams found in 2010 that babies just under 1,500 grams, who get extra care, were less likely to die in their first year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13760
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Barreca and colleagues answered in 2011 that babies at round weights come disproportionately from poorer, less healthy births, and that setting them aside shrinks that benefit sharply.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:nrcmkq'
    male|a||The original authors replied that the benefit shrinks but stays large, above all in hospitals with weaker units for newborns.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7ndt3p'
    male|a||What would settle it is weights recorded without rounding, so that no babies pile up at the line.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ibn8b3'
    male|a||So the second test asks who could reach the line. A birthday cannot be moved, a booking or a reported income can, and a count at the line is the first way to tell which you have.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7uzizt'
    male|a||Turning sixty-five does not insure everyone who lacked cover, and it changes the insurance of many who already had some. So what exactly does the drop at sixty-five measure?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Call crossing the line Z, and having any insurance at all D: both are switches, zero or one, for each patient.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1quvlzl'
    'male|a||Among the emergency patients, crossing sixty-five cut the share with no insurance from about ten percent to two. So D jumps by eight points, with a standard error of two tenths: most were covered already.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:yj9g18'
    male|a||The outcome Y is death within a week, and if coverage is what saves lives, the line works through D.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8e3e4q'
    'male|a||And Y fell by one point at the line, with a standard error of two tenths: the effect of crossing itself, diluted, since only eight in a hundred had their coverage change.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ui699l'
    'male|a||If D is the only road, the fuzzy design undoes that dilution: it divides the jump in Y by the jump in D, the same ratio as an instrumental variable, with crossing the line as the instrument.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:efrpf6'
    'male|a||If coverage were the only road, that is minus one over eight hundredths: twelve and a half points fewer deaths among the newly insured.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:v21h8t'
    male|a||Check that against the patients themselves. Uninsured patients just under sixty-five died within a week about five percent of the time.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:3il0jx'
    male|a||Coverage cannot push a risk below zero, so eight in a hundred, each spared at most five percent, account for at most four tenths of a point.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:192ao05'
    male|a||The rest must travel another road. At sixty-five nearly half of these patients switch to Medicare as their main insurer, often from plans that limited care, and they get more done in hospital.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tzq6eo'
    male|a||That road bypasses D, so dividing by the jump in D hands all of the drop to coverage alone, and the ratio comes out impossibly large.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1y43p5h'
    male|a||A fuzzy ratio is honest only when crossing the line moves the outcome through the treatment alone, and when no one is pushed out of treatment by crossing.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:re49l0'
    'male|a||When both hold, the ratio is the effect for the compliers at the cutoff: the people whose coverage changed because they turned sixty-five, and nobody else.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1rcyahf'
    'male|a||Card, Dobkin and Maestas did not divide. They reported the drop as the effect of reaching Medicare age: more coverage for a few, and better coverage for many.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:f6y370'
    male|a||A new case. A clinic offers a free follow-up visit to patients with a risk score above 50. At 50 the share who get a visit jumps from 10 to 50 percent, and readmissions fall by 2 points. What does the ratio estimate?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 17440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:zfhxw1'
    male|a||Two points over forty points of take-up is five, and it speaks only for patients who got the visit because they crossed 50, if the score does nothing else at 50.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||A discontinuity is believable when its answer holds as the window changes, not at one chosen width.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||It needs a line nobody could choose their side of, and a count of people at the line is the first check.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fmcvm2'
    male|a||And a fuzzy ratio needs every road from the line to pass through the treatment; then it speaks for the people the line moved.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jgkbtu'
    male|a||So does Medicare save lives? For emergency patients at sixty-five, the drop survives the window and the count.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:by8atj'
    'male|a||And the third test says what it is: the effect of reaching Medicare, better cover as much as any cover, not of being insured alone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1bkvtqq'
